# Ex6a  cluster of 20 water molecules cut from ice, 400 K, Nose-Hoover chain thermostat
# (a) ab initio MD, PBE/def2-SVP, small cluster
# 200 steps x 0.5 fs = 100 fs. The ORCA manual recommends a time step of at most 0.5 fs
# for systems containing hydrogen.
#
# Cell Sphere cx, cy, cz, r: soft harmonic wall that keeps molecules evaporating from the hot cluster
# from flying away. "Sphere of size 50 A" is read as diameter 50 A -> r = 25 A. The centre is the
# geometric centre of the cluster (the xyz is not centred at the origin); the cluster itself has a
# radius of only 6.4 A, so the wall acts only on molecules that leave the cluster.
! MD PBE def2-SVP def2/J

%maxcore 6000

%md
  Timestep   0.5_fs
  Initvel    400_K
  Thermostat NHC 400_K Timecon 10.0_fs
  Cell       Sphere 1.901, 3.292, 3.750, 25.0
  Dump       Position Stride 1 Filename "ex6a_trajectory_DFT_PBE.xyz"
  Run        200
end

* xyzfile 0 1 ../ex6a_water_cluster_20H2O_for_DFT.xyz
